		*html
			<div class="full-rules-box">
			<p><a href="http://clearerresearch.org/">Clearer Research</a> is a meta-science project aimed at supporting and improving psychological science. Our work spans several areas, including:</p>
			<p>● Combatting the replication crisis and exploring where there is opportunity for improvement in current research practices, by running rapid replications and conducting careful analyses of recently published psychological studies (<a href="https://replications.clearerthinking.org/">Transparent Replications</a>)</p>
			<p>● Developing easy-to-use, browser-based tools for conducting social science research, such as:<br>
			&nbsp; ○ <a href="https://www.positly.com/">Positly.com</a>: A platform for recruiting study participants<br>
			&nbsp; ○ <a href="https://www.guidedtrack.com/">GuidedTrack</a>: A platform for building studies, surveys, educational modules, apps, tools, and prototypes without hiring a programmer<br>
			&nbsp; ○ <a href="https://www.hypothesize.io/">Hypothesize.io</a>: A platform for analyzing and visualizing data, with support for more than 100 statistical methods and built-in explanations<br>
			&nbsp; ○ <a href="https://personalitymap.io/">PersonalityMap.io</a>: A platform that lets you search and explore over 1 million empirical correlations between human traits</p>
			<p>● Initiatives designed to identify and promote high-impact research directions, including the Unanswered Questions in Psychology Prize.</p>
			
			<p>Clearer Research grew out of a sister project, <a href="https://www.clearerthinking.org/">Clearer Thinking</a> (established in 2013 and since then featured in different media outlets such as Scientific American, Vox, WSJ, the New York Times, and others), which develops resources (educational tools, articles, and a podcast) about psychology and critical thinking for a general audience. In contrast, Clearer Research is focused on offering value to the academic community.</p>
			
			<p>Clearer Research is funded by grants, donations, self-funding, and Clearer Thinking subscriptions.</p>
			</div>


