----------------------------------
-- How it works
----------------------------------

*html
	<div style="height: 40px !important;"></div>
	<h2>How it works</h2>
	
/*Submission:*/ You submit what you see as being an important, unanswered question pertaining to the subject matter of psychology. You have the option to include a brief explanation of why the question is important, if you like. Anyone can submit, though we expect the substantial majority of submissions to come from academic psychologists.

/*Judging:*/ After the submission deadline (November 10th, 2026), eligible submitted questions will be deduplicated and reduced to a manageable longlist by the Clearer Research team. The resulting set of questions will then be voted on by academic psychologists only (all current and former academic psychologists will be eligible to vote) to determine the winners.

/*Awards:*/ Each participant who submitted a question that's judged to be among the "most important" based on the votes of academic psychologists will be awarded the Unanswered Questions in Psychology Prize and $400 USD.

/*Publication:*/ We will publish the final list of winning questions, along with the names of those who submitted them (except for those who opted to remain anonymous), on the [Clearer Research|https://v0-university-website-redesign-ruddy.vercel.app/#resources] and [Clearer Thinking|https://www.clearerthinking.org] websites and newsletter (our typical reach is 250,000 people) and pursue press attention. We are also interested in collaborating with any winners on an article for academic publication about the project and results, with details to be discussed.

*html
