	*html
		<div class="specification-note">
			<p><b>Questions must...</b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>pertain to the subject matter of psychology, broadly construed.</li>
			<li><b>not</b> pertain to meta-level questions about psychology as a discipline (e.g., "How do we improve replicability?", "Should we get rid of p-values?", or "How do we increase interdisciplinary collaboration?" are beyond the scope of this prize. This exclusion does not reflect a judgment about their importance).</li>
			</ul>
		
			<p><b>Questions may...</b></p>
			<ul>
			<li>draw on or intersect with adjacent fields such as neuroscience, philosophy, economics, or public policy. As long as they remain substantively about psychological phenomena.</li>
			<li>be very broad, very narrow, or anywhere in between.</li>
			<li>be empirical, theoretical, or conceptual. They are not required to be currently answerable, or even answerable in principle.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

